  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Peace Building Mount Hoyo/Ituri 2022-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Main objective: To provide a multi-sectoral response for the effective return of peace and the resumption of socio-economic life in the area around the Mont Hoyo, Ituri Province in DR Congo.
The expected effects for the target group of the Project are (Outcome) to contribute to a sense of normality, economic empowerment, and active participation for people in the area.
The planned main products and/or services of the Project are the following outputs: 1) Rehabilitation of 13 km of access road + one bridge in the Mount Hoyo forest reserve (employment of people vulnerable to recruitment in local armed rebel groups); 2) Operational costs for one ambulating health clinic; 3) Distribution of 1500 farming kits; ; 4) peace seminars with local civil society groups and local leaderss; 5) 4 football tournaments and 4 drama seminars.The intended target group is local population affected by insurgency and returning IDPs, local chiefs, leaders of women&#x2019;s groups, local church leaders and leaders of local NGOs, local youth and villagers (also as spectators and players.</narrative>
  </description>
